    "answer": {
      "short": "$987\\times121=119427$. Partial products: $987$, $19740$, $98700$.",
      "worked": "The tens partial product has five digits, so twice the multiplicand has four digits. The multiplicand is therefore at least 500. Its product with each of the multiplier’s unknown digits has only three digits, so both unknown multiplier digits must be 1. The multiplier is 121.\n\nThe hundreds partial product is therefore the multiplicand followed by two zeros. Its given 8 fixes the multiplicand’s tens digit. Checking the remaining digits against the sum’s given 9 and 2 gives 987.\n\n$$\\begin{array}{crrrrrr}&&&&9&8&7\\\\\\times&&&&1&2&1\\\\\\hline&&&&9&8&7\\\\&&1&9&7&4&0\\\\&&9&8&7&0&0\\\\\\hline&1&1&9&4&2&7\\\\\\hline\\hline\\end{array}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
